--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SignalLogViewerPage.tsx is the "query signal history from Postgres" workspace. It sets a
PageContainer (title="Signal Log Viewer", subtitle="Query signal history from Postgres",
actions=<VehicleSelect/>, copyLink), reads the global useSelectedVehicle() store, and
shows the query failure (if any) in an <AlertBanner variant="danger">. When no vehicle is
selected (vehicleId === 0) it renders an <EmptyState icon={<Activity/>}
title=signalLog.noVehicle message=signalLog.noVehicleDesc/>. Otherwise it draws ONE
<GlassPanel> (the parity manifest's single panel "GlassPanel1") holding the shared
SignalSelector (max=null), a Time-Range RangePicker, a Per-Page Select, the Query button
and the "{n} records" caption; below it, a pre-query <EmptyState icon={<Database/>}
title="Select signals and click Query" message="Choose one or more signals, …"/> until the
user clicks Query, then the shared <SignalHistoryTable/>.

Its declared data source is useSignals (GET /signals/{vehicleId}/available — the selector
catalog). The deferred history query is a useQuery({ enabled: queryKey !== null }) that
fans out one request() per selected signal to GET /signals/{id}/{sig}/history?from=&to=,
flat-maps + adapts the typed {ts,value} points into SignalLogEntry rows via
adaptSignalHistoryResp (web/src/components/SignalQueryControls.tsx), sorts them newest-first,
and paginates purely locally by slicing the fetched batch. Parity manifest: 1 panel, 4 data
states (loading/empty/error/success), 12 strings — requiredCount=17.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 feature-views already exist and are reused verbatim (DRY, ADR-006):
  - io.teslasync.android.featureviews.signalselector.SignalSelector — the controlled
    multi-select (options/value/onChange/max), the web SignalSelector port.
  - io.teslasync.android.featureviews.signalhistorytable.SignalHistoryTable — the
    presentational history table; its UiState<SignalHistoryData> overload renders the
    loading skeleton / empty / error+retry / content states, the web SignalHistoryTable port.
  - io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.vehicleselect.VehicleSelect — the store-bound picker.
  - io.teslasync.android.components.forms.DateRangeFilter — the Time-Range control.
This page is their host: it sets the header, owns the deferred-query client state + the
per-signal fan-out + the local pagination through a page ViewModel, and renders the web
layout — never re-implementing the selector/table (mirrors the sibling
telemetry/SignalGapDetectorPage, which embeds the shared SignalCatalogPanel).

