Notes:
  - i18n catalog: the web literal-as-key strings (Signal Log Viewer, Per Page, Time Range, …)
    and the signalLog.* / error.loadFailed namespaced keys are resolved on web via t() with
    inline defaults. en.json is outside this artifact's allowed files, so the Android catalog
    receives those exact web defaults under the generator's androidName() resource names
    (honest disclosure; same hand-edit pattern as the sibling SignalGapDetector keys).
    MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled in the app lint config, so the ar/he
    English-fallback entries are accepted.
  - Routing: page("signalLog","/signal-log",NavGroup.Telemetry) already exists in
    Destinations.kt (metadata-only); this artifact only attaches the host (no route-table
    change).
  - Data wiring: the Android DI graph (DataContainer) wires no TelemetryStore, so the host
    builds a page-local HttpTelemetryRepository from the shared client + offline cache the
    container exposes (the SignalGapDetector/RegenEfficiency precedent). The view performs no
    HTTP — the ViewModel drives the source.
  - SI: the table renders no unit-bearing field here; the shared SignalHistoryTable keeps raw
    SI and formats values/timestamps at its own boundary (Phase-42/48). The Time-Range dates
    are converted to from/to ISO instants at the display boundary (signalLogIsoRange, S5).
  - a11y/theme: PageTitle heading + BodyText subtitle + MetricLabel/Caption via MaterialTheme
    tokens; AlertBanner/EmptyState/Select/Button/SignalSelector/SignalHistoryTable/VehicleSelect
    supply their own content descriptions + dynamic/dark theme (ADR-015). No hardcoded
    colors/typography; Compose-native only (no webview).

